[Music]  [Music]  my name is Rick Brown owner of venture  sixty north Adventure Center in Seward  Alaska  I've been guiding here since the early  90s I've lived here permanently since  2003 and have been guiding in the  glaciers all that time  normally I think that Park will tell you  that it retreats about 150 feet per year  right now they're looking at 10 to 15  feet per day  you're seeing the big crevasses that  used to be blue up on top of the  compression zones now down in the Toyota  glacier just falling over  something that normally would take  hundreds of years we're seeing probably  in a matter of a year or two we're just  watching the transformation happened in  front of our eyes right now  as you drive into our park you'll see  the signs that mark different points  where the glacier had traveled during  the 1800s all the way back to the early  nineteen hundred's  things that used to take hundreds of  years is actually now only taken months  we're seeing a change in the wildlife  we have villages that are being  relocated  we get storms up here that if they were  happening down in the lower 48 we name  them something  our ten-year floods are happening every  other year now  you can drive to our town and look at  what's going on and if you can't see  what's happening then I think that you  must be blind  [Music]  we're running a snowcat out here  normally I would need a plow here in my  office and we needed a lot more  [Music]  I  hope that the people that come to Alaska  to visit us they take time to try to  understand what it is they're seeing  this place will not stay the same is  going to be different but I just hope  that we just learned how to take care of  it  [Music]  you know I have four daughters and a  bunch of grandkids as I sit here and  talk about this I wonder what they will  see if they come back after I'm gone  that's my concern is for the future  wondering how this climate thing is  going to work out for them  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  you  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  you  [Music]

